[38;2;124;124;124mActually, I need to be careful about definitions. A "topological manifold" of [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdimension n is a second-countable Hausdorff space that is locally Euclidean of [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdimension n. Compactness is given.[0m

